.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
An unsigned stream says nothing of its sender: anyone with a recipient's
public key can write one, and every recipient holds the file key and can
write another stream to the same header.
Only
.Fn nqkmdfin
with the sender's
.Fa pk ,
returning
.Dv NQOK ,
shows that the sender signed this plaintext for these recipients.
.Pp
Chunks come out before the stream is known to be whole: a truncated or
altered stream is reported only at the failing chunk or at
.Fn nqkmdfin .
Act on the plaintext, or show it, only after that.
.Pp
The header shows how many recipients there are, the KEM of each and 8
bytes of the hash of each public key, enough to tell whether a known key
is among them.
The plaintext's length, to within the chunk, is not hidden.
